  "description": "CR 717.2a / CR 603.10 the level-2 section's trigger fires on the very activation that grants it",
  "note": "'Becomes level N' is on none of CR 603.10's look-back exceptions, so the trigger is checked against the abilities existing after the level change, which CR 717.2a's static half has just granted. Lightning Bolt in alice's graveyard and Divination in bob's: both pass the slot's instant-or-sorcery filter, so only 'your graveyard' (CR 400.1) tells them apart. bob's own Stormchaser's Talent, already level 2, holds the same trigger throughout: one matching any Class's level change would return bob's Divination on alice's activation. The Haskell test writes bob's level and places his Raise Dead; here bob levels on his turn with an empty graveyard, his trigger finding no target, then casts Divination.",
